  "notes": "Distinct review of all 240 literal statements and the De la Court text, Secrétan scholarship and Klerk abstract. Qualified any supposedly categorical anti-monarchism: Klerk finds the critique targets coercive princely war politics and concentration of military power rather than monarchy as such. Provincial liberty is not universal modern democracy; useful foreigners and religious toleration do not establish unrestricted residence and welfare. Guild/monopoly opposition is doctrinal and is not copied from actual colonial company practice. Assessed each neutral for its identified competing commitments, including temperament, bodily experimentation and fiscal/social safeguards. No country vectors used to choose responses. All 240 IDs are educated assumptions, exhaustively recorded in the separate review. Validation is structural, not an empirical certification. Similarity decisions follow validation without retuning responses. Reviewed all neutral-density warnings against individual competing commitments; none represents an unanswered item. Exact neutral IDs and validator warnings are recorded in the separate review.",
